\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Trajectory}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}
\tag{reinforcement-learning}

\p{A \strong{public trajectory} is the stopped sequence}

##{
  \tau=(q,O_0,A_0,O_1,A_1,\ldots,A_{T-1},O_T,Y).
}

\p{Its probability law is induced jointly by the task law, initial-state law,
environment kernel, policy, stopping rule, and all declared random seeds. This
is the usual reinforcement-learning trajectory specialized to an explicit
public record; compare \citef{murphy2024reinforcement}.}

\p{The trajectory does not contain optimizer state or later reuse metadata.
Those belong to the training protocol. Keeping them separate allows one
completed interaction to be selected for several update attempts without
changing the historical event.}
